  "review_conclusions": [
    "Scene contracts own descriptors, structured paths, generic values and opaque world identity; actual ECS storage, registration and handle allocation remain caller-owned.",
    "EntityPath and ComponentPropertyPath parsing, capacity helpers and raw-text coupling were traced through World consumers; preexisting roundtrip BUG/TODO remain open and all source-string predicates preserve their actual booleans.",
    "Mobility virtual-field parsing borrows normalized input and reports conversions before mutation; generated reflection operates on a cloned component, then routes through checked World::set_mobility rather than bypassing its admission.",
    "Physics metadata is authored shared configuration with serde defaults. Runtime/provider admission is separate; Jolt applies only selected material fields and supports explicit primitive inertia through a scalar uniform multiplier.",
    "LevelManager creation publishes after runtime preparation; asset calls validate active project generation, capture snapshot/project/URI before asynchronous persistence, and return observer tickets whose timeout does not cancel work.",
    "SystemStage::ORDER is shared by native ordinal decoding; the fixed driver wraps each complete FIXED_LOOP in a begin/commit-or-abort transaction. WorldHandle is a transparent numeric identity and has no implicit registry lookup.",
    "All existing code, strings, assertions, DSL and comments remain unchanged. Context-only plugin risks were neither edited nor booked as formal coverage."
  ],
